text:
- **Session ↔ held instance:** one `escher_driver::Session` booted through `seven_guis::stand` holds state, focus, ids, CRUD rows and timer time across commands and reads as a fresh boot, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_state.rs:56-169; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_ids.rs:52-141; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_fresh.rs:39-117); a step run through `Session::act` returns settled — the Timer's delayed update present, an idle step changing nothing, a write made while mounting present — or `SessionError::NotSettled(Busy::Render)` at the bound with the instance still readable, in both layout modes and with no sleep or clock read in the check (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_settle.rs:35-174; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_settle.rs:277-312); since 2026-10-20-load-wait an acting step that meets a load in flight waits for it up to `LOAD_WAIT` (5 s of wall time), settling again every 10 ms and moving no time — `stand_load_wait` 2 through `Session::run` in both layout modes: a load answered at 200 ms ends the `click` settled with its content on screen, a load never answered ends it at the bound `settled` false with `busy` `Loads`, `harness().time()` unmoved in both (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_load_wait.rs:107-164); a caller-built `Call` run through `Session::run` on a held session — `snapshot`, and `click` · `type` · `press` · `advance` · `scroll`, the first two and the last addressed by stable id alone — returns after settle with the diff of the snapshots taken before and after it, equal to the check's own `before.diff(&after)` and across the two layout modes; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` returns the screen, or the element its optional id names, as a PNG equal to the harness's raster and changes nothing — `has_changes` false, focus and the diff unchanged
 — an element shot's id refused `not-found` or `stale` and one cropping to no pixel `off-screen` with the instance unchanged, and a password typed through the driver never leaving as pixels (`stand_act_screenshot`); a refused call — any of the eight causes (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18, `advance` accepted on every session): `unknown-verb`, `malformed`, `not-found`, `stale`, `disabled`, `off-screen`, `covered` and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `fonts-unavailable` — leaves the instance unchanged and reads as a text holding none of the bytes the call supplied, and for each of the five the executor detects on the screen a refused `click` and a refused `type` leave the snapshot and both focus readings equal;
 a `scroll` is refused for none of the three checks that stand in front of a click and says in its result whether its element is then in view — on the stand a CRUD row past its list's box is refused `off-screen`, brought into view by `scroll` and then clicked, the row's centre read against the list's `bounds` taken once, before the scroll — a scroll of the list's content does not move them; a password typed through the driver occurs 0 times in what the call returns and reads `MASKED_VALUE`; with no sleep and no wall-clock read in the checks — bar two recorded exceptions whose subject is wall time: `stand_virtual_clock`'s one 800 ms sleep, taken so a shot after a scroll is read to repeat across wall time until `advance` moves the fade, and, since 2026-10-20-load-wait, `stand_load_wait`, which reads `Instant::now()` around its call to measure the load wait against `LOAD_WAIT` and whose in-file `LateNet` stand-in answers from its own thread after a 200 ms sleep; `stand_load_page` reads no clock and sleeps nowhere, the 200 ms sleep its click waits out through `LOAD_WAIT` being the stand's own `LoadNet`'s (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_load_page.rs:35-111), and `stand_cells_served` moves time by `advance` alone — and in the Timer flow no pass but the driver's; and with escher's sink installed at `info` each call run through `Session::run` — ran or refused
 — leaves exactly one `escher_driver` line holding fixed words and counts only (its verb, a refused call's cause, an acting call's settle reading and the three lengths of the returned diff) and none of the ids, names, values or typed text it handled, and at the default level no driver line — `stand_act_spans`, each reading made in a re-run child because the level is read when the sink is installed; and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli a `type` replaces what a filled control holds and an empty text clears it, a masked control's written form holds the mask and never the typed text (`stand_act_filled`), and since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit the two engine readings 2026-10-10-driver-cli pinned are fixed in the engine and their checks restated — a scrolled box reads the same `bounds` before and after its content is scrolled, the scroll's diff does not name it, and a `click` naming the box lands on the row at its centre (`stand_act_scroll`);
 a click on a Cells cell inside a scrolled box right after `scroll` lands on the shown overlay scrollbar, which takes it as a thumb drag and dispatches nothing, and a pointer left on the thumb keeps the scrollbar shown, so an `advance` past the fade comes before the click (`stand_cells_served`; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_cells_served.rs:216-232); the keyboard walks to a cell and commits a value read in the first part, `press` walking and opening the editor, `type` supplying the characters and `press` committing (`stand_cells_served`; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_cells_served.rs:179-214), and a click inside a cell's own open editor returns early, so the text typed there stays (examples/seven_guis/src/tasks/cells.rs:425-433); a button lying where a scrolled-out row extends is clicked, its handler runs and no row's, and after the accepted click the clicked button reads `focused` and is the tree's focus (`stand_act_obstructed`, restated at 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness); two readings stay as measured, each stated in `covered`'s fixed meaning, which also says an option of a closed select lies under it and to click the select first, then the option: a box with no width or no height is hit at its centre on the element that holds it, so `covered` can read where nothing covers it (`stand_act_ids`), and a box clipped on one axis stops a hit at its whole padding box, so a target lying outside it along the axis it does not clip is refused `covered` though it shows, the instance unchanged, in both layout modes (`stand_act_obstructed`'s sixth test; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_obstructed.rs:560-605; packages/escher-driver/src/refusal.rs:75-81);
 and since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states an acting call returns the node it changed with its `selected` or `invalid` reading as it reads after the step — a flight-type choice the select `flight-type` with its `value` and its two options with their `selected` reading (the stand stating no `aria-pressed`, `pressed` pinned on a fixture by `accessibility_states`), a row click the row selected and the row it leaves not selected, a typed start date the field invalid or not — each diff equal across the two layout modes (`stand_act_states`); a `click` on a translated button is accepted and lands, and its snapshot `bounds` read where it shows, in both layout modes (`stand_act_transformed`; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_transformed.rs:81-193); a `type` on a single-choice select chooses the first option whose label starts with the text — accepted and settled, its diff naming the select with `value` in `differs` and the two options whose `selected` moved, the select's options read as its children named by their labels, a disabled select skipped by the Tab walk and refused, in both layout modes (`stand_act_select`; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_select.rs:85-270) (the sixteen `stand_act_*` files, §1) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md, the three state readings at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md, the two fixed readings at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/report.md, the detected causes and `scroll` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, the command span's line at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md

- **Session host ↔ what it writes:** `stand_session_quiet` proves the session library and the harness path write nothing of the screen — typed text, a stable id, an accessible name — to stdout, to stderr or into the state directory, whose listing is `session.sock` alone, and that nothing on that path reads `RUST_LOG`: its host is the re-run test binary, which installs no log sink, so the `RUST_LOG=trace` it is started with is inert.
 It does not cover a host that installs escher's sink; that host is covered by seven_guis' `host_log` — the real `escher-session` binary on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace`, its needles read from the stand booted in the test's own process (at least 15 stable ids asserted, 16 read; the CRUD row and label texts), both streams drained by a thread each from the spawn on, the session reached with `attach` under a 60 s bound (never `start`, which reads no stream), driven since 2026-10-10-driver-cli by three calls through the binary as a client — a `snapshot`, a `click` and a `type` of a sentinel — and stopped with `stop`: exit 0, empty stdout, no state directory, at least one stderr line, every stderr line carrying `service.name=seven_guis`, exactly one `command` span line per call, and no id, no name and no occurrence of the typed sentinel anywhere on stderr, under the `-p seven_guis` build and the workspace build, a failure printing a kind and a count only — seen red on the unfixed sink (16 of 16 id needles and 6 of 6 name needles in 1501 stderr lines) — and by `telemetry_drop`, which proves the sink writes nothing for a third-party target at any level, native and bridged, under a `RUST_LOG` directive naming it; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the binary's `mcp` role is covered by seven_guis' `mcp_log` — at `RUST_LOG=trace`, under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build, 0 typed-sentinel occurrences, 0 id needles and 0 name needles on stderr, one `tool_call` line per call with only its stated field names, and protocol lines only on stdout (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:53-315); since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot `host_log` and `mcp_log` also drive shots and read 0 occurrences of a shot's first 64 base64 characters on stderr at `trace`, under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:514-527;
 examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:190-203), and each also drives one `lint` and one `snapshot` part read — `host_log` seven calls and 7 command-span lines, `mcp_log` ten tool calls and 8 `command` lines — still reading 0 needles on stderr at `trace`; `host_log` holds 5 tests and `mcp_log` 3. A paged `part` read through the `escher-session` host's own sink is read by `host_log`'s fourth test, which runs `serve cells` at `RUST_LOG=trace`, commits a sentinel into a part-2 cell and reads `snapshot --part 2`, 0 id and 0 name needles under both builds, its needles from `common::cells_needles(part)` (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:137-280; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:455-484); the in-process capture reads one too (`stand_act_spans`, §1).
 By level, both sink-installing binaries read 0 ids and 0 names at the default level, `info`, `debug` and `trace` — the windowed stand by the evidence instrument on the dev host, not by a standing check; since 2026-10-14-quality-gates the windowed binary built with the workspace, on the host's display, a client's own stderr and the host on flows beyond the three CRUD commands are read by build and level too, 28 runs with 0 needles, by the same kind of instrument (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/evidence/stderr-by-level.md), and a recording session's clients are read by a standing check
 — seven_guis' `cfg(unix)` `a_recording_sessions_clients_log_nothing_of_it_at_trace` runs each client command as a process through `common::run` at `RUST_LOG=trace` — `start crud --record`, `type --id crud-name --text {SENTINEL}`, `snapshot`, `snapshot --part 1`, `lint` and `stop` — in the state directories `hl-client` and `hl-client-rec` under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, guarded by `common::Started { dir, pid }`, and over all their stderr reads 0 id, 0 name, 0 sentinel, 0 recording-path and 0 `recorded_needles` occurrences under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build, compiled for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` too (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:45-135);
 typed text is measured on the session host's log since 2026-10-10-driver-cli — 0 occurrences of a typed sentinel at `trace`, as `host_log` above — and stays unmeasured on the windowed binary's; it was first measured in process, where `stand_act_spans` runs the driver's `type` with escher's sink installed over a capture and reads 0 occurrences of the typed text, 0 of 36 ids and 0 of 8 names; since 2026-10-19-session-recording `host_log` and `mcp_log` each also run a recording host and a recording `mcp` role at `RUST_LOG=trace` and read 0 of the recording needles (the kept check's names and its directory's name) on stderr, the span counts unchanged, the kept check living in the launcher's recording directory and the state directory still `session.sock` alone; a full recorded Cells session keeps a check of 312,431 bytes and the load page's 1,660, under the 1,048,576-byte bound, measured by a probe through the built binary, no standing check (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-25-cold-agent-bar/report.md) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_quiet.rs:30-115; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:33-608; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:39-43; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:59-66; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_drop.rs:16-67; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_spans.rs:1-24; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md, the in-process capture at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md)

- **Command line (`escher-session`, unix only; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli):** each driver command is run as a process of the package's own binary against a host its `start` command spawned — `cli_commands` (15): each of the six served tasks — the four lean tasks, `cells` and `load` — starts, answers and stops; `snapshot --part` read by number answers one uncoloured JSON line, status 0, and `--part` 0, 1001 and `x` exit 1 with a line equal to `Refusal::malformed(fault).to_json()`, nothing typed written back (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:299-344); since 2026-10-14-quality-gates a run with its stdout closed before it starts keeps its ending's status — `help` 0, `snapshot` with no session 3 with exactly `NoSession`'s message — printing no panic and writing nothing typed back (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:733-758); each of the eight instance-level verbs is accepted and answers exactly its fields — since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` answering status `0` and one line whose `png`, decoded by a hand base64 reader and checked by its PNG header, equals the PNG `Session::run` returns in process (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:346-418); a hosted `lint` answers status `0` and one line `{"findings":[]}` (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:466-487); a snapshot is the in-process text as one line inside its 10,000-byte budget (832 · 1,403 · 1,368 · 2,208 bytes on the four lean tasks, line break included, as measured at .andromeda/runs/2026-10-25T17-25-04-wrap/snapshot-sizes.md); a call a target cannot take is refused with its cause, status `1`; a call the schema refuses reaches no session; a command with no session is a session error, status `3`; a line that is no command is a usage error, status `2`; Tab on a fresh boot moves focus to `back-btn` alone;
 since 2026-10-12-self-description `help` answers status `0` and one line equal to `describe()`, reaching no session, every cause the binary provokes (`unknown-verb`, `malformed`, `disabled`, `not-found`, `off-screen`, `stale`) reads `remedy` equal to its cause's, and a state directory of 94 bytes as given starts and stops while one of 95 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status `3`, its message naming 94 and its remedy the table's, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, off Linux one of 90 bytes starts and stops while one of 91 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status `3`, with no path in the message — its one witness the fork's CI run on the macOS leg, CI#38642493451, job 116123587286, `cli_commands` 11 passed on `aarch64-apple-darwin` (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:766-770) — `cli_flow` (2): the two shell flows `counter.sh` (8 steps) and `flight.sh` (7) complete under plain `sh` and leave nothing, and a flow handed a binary that answers nothing says which step failed and stops its session — and `host_timer` (1): the timer host moved by a hosted `advance` with no sleep, reporting exactly the `ms` asked; the fork's CI run on the macOS leg is the one witness of the select-all modifier and of the two flows there (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:134-664; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:665-839; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_flow.rs:31-88; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_timer.rs:22-126; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md, the two new tests at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md);
 since 2026-10-19-session-recording `start <task> --record <dir>` run as a process keeps one `0600` check in a `0700` directory, the state directory gone after `stop`, a group-open recording directory refused status `3` with nothing spawned (seven_guis `recording`), and `cli_commands` reads the usage line naming `--record` on `start`, the host role and the `mcp` role, a misplaced `--record` a usage error, status `2`, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay `recording`'s `the_committed_checks_are_what_the_binary_records` runs `record_checks.sh` — a command-line session (`start counter --record` · `snapshot` · `click counter-increment` · `advance 600` · `click counter-increment` · `snapshot` · `stop`) and an MCP one (`initialize` … `scroll counter-increment` · `snapshot` · `stop`) — through the binary and reads both kept checks byte-equal to `tests/blitz-tests/checks/counter-{cli,mcp}.json`, the scripts holding no `screenshot` step since a shot's PNG bytes differ by OS (CI#39225375577) (examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:205-262; examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:264-304; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:628-638)
